   "final_text": "The feed had one event, a termination, and I've handled it in every system. No new events came in during about 45 minutes of checking, and nothing I started is still waiting on a response.\n\n**Case case-d9bc1d97: Ravi Carter (E1002), Software Engineer, left 2026-10-30**\nThe termination was already in effect when I picked it up on 2026-11-02, but his account was still enabled and had one active session. So I removed his access before taking any irreversible step.\n\n- **Legal hold:** none.\n- **Identity (acct-8d88348a):**\n  - Disabled the account and ended the active session.\n  - Removed him from the All-Staff, Eng-Git and VPN-Users groups.\n  - Turned his mailbox into a shared mailbox, so his email is kept.\n  - Removed his Office-E3 license.\n  - I did not delete the account. The organization's policy is that rehires get their old account back, and nothing required deleting it.\n- **Finance:**\n  - His one pending expense report (exp-3b1a11df, $936) was closed for final processing before Avery Carter, the manager it was waiting on, had approved it. That manager is still active, so nobody needed to take over his approvals.\n  - He doesn't approve expenses for anyone else.\n  - His corporate card was already off.\n  - I requested his final paycheck, which can't be undone.\n- **Equipment:** he has engineering equipment on record, so I opened recovery ticket tkt-09b4e5d2. It's open, and getting the equipment back is tracked in the ticketing system.\n\nThe expense report was closed without approval, so someone should check that the $936 is still dealt with in final processing."
